---
title: "Tooltips"
---

Tooltips display additional information for cells, column headers and the grid's own controls on hover, keyboard focus or touch.

The example below combines cell and header tooltips using fixed text, callbacks and a custom component on Total Medals, alongside the built-in tooltips on the pagination, column menu and side bar, all shown on hover or keyboard focus.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tooltips" name="tooltips-demo" /%}

## Column Tooltips

Set what cell and header tooltips show using fixed text, the cell value or a callback. [Column Tooltips](./tooltips-columns/) also covers blank values, truncated text and row groups.

## Showing & Hiding

Control when tooltips appear with [Show and Hide Delay](./tooltips-show-hide/) and the [Tooltip Trigger](./tooltips-show-hide/#tooltip-trigger), which selects hover, keyboard focus or both. [Interactive Tooltips](./tooltips-show-hide/#interactive-tooltips) let users select text or use controls inside a tooltip, and [Touch Devices](./tooltips-show-hide/#touch-devices) show tooltips on long press.

## Positioning

Choose where tooltips appear with [Positioning](./tooltips-positioning/), including [Arrows](./tooltips-positioning/#arrows) and [Mouse Tracking](./tooltips-positioning/#mouse-tracking).

## Custom Tooltip Component

Supply a [Custom Tooltip Component](./component-tooltip/) to change what a tooltip contains and how it looks.

## Built-in Control Tooltips

The grid's own controls, such as pagination, the column menu and the side bar, show [Built-in Control Tooltips](./tooltips-built-in/), which can be suppressed or customised.

## Opting Out of Grid Tooltips {% #browser-tooltip %}

Set `enableBrowserTooltips: true` to use the browser's native tooltips instead of the grid's. Custom components, delays, positioning and the immediate-focus behaviour do not apply, and built-in controls fall back to native `title` hints.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    enableBrowserTooltips: true,
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Default Browser Tooltip" name="default-tooltip" exampleHeight=250 /%}
